    "Description": "The is a carousel map from a bird-eye perspective of the Pullen Park Carousel. In a box in the lower right corner is the label, \"PULLEN PARK CAROSEL [sic] RESTORATION PROJECT Spring 1976 Scale 1/3 = 1\" A large circle is segmented and numbered, and stickers, writing in pen, and tape are in the section to map the locations of the carousel animals. In the upper right corner and bottom edge of the paper are keys explaining which animals correspond to the letters and roman numerals on the map.",
